<title>KUWAIT: Fire breaks out near Kuwait's al-Magwa oil field.</title>
<headline>Fire breaks out near Kuwait's al-Magwa oil field.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fire broke out in an oil lake east of al-Magwa oil field in Kuwait on Sunday without causing damage to oil installations or injuries before it was brought under control, the official Kuwait News Agency (KUNA) said.</p>
<p>KUNA quoted a Kuwait Oil Company official as saying the fire started when cluster bombs left over from the 1991 Gulf War were being detonated set fire to dry grass.</p>
<p>Oil lakes were formed by oil leaking and gushing from oil installations and wells damaged during the 1991 Gulf War against Iraq.</p>
</text>
